This product is a TypeScript/Node.js port of "Goose", an article/content
extraction library, and includes substantial code, algorithms, and test
fixtures translated or adapted from earlier ports in this lineage:

  - Goose (original)
    Java, later Scala. Licensed to Gravity.com under one or more
    contributor license agreements.
    https://github.com/GravityLabs/goose

  - python-goose
    Python port written by Xavier Grangier for Recrutae.
    https://github.com/grangier/python-goose
    Stopword lists (src/resources/text/stopwords-*.txt), the known-image
    CSS heuristics list (src/resources/images/known-image-css.txt), and
    the HTML/JSON test fixtures under test/fixtures/ are carried over
    from this project.

  - node-unfluff
    An earlier, independent JavaScript port/reimagining of goose's
    heuristics for Node.js, written by Adam Geitgey. Consulted as prior
    art and a reference for what a JS-idiomatic API can look like.
    https://github.com/ageitgey/node-unfluff

  - goose-ts (this project)
    TypeScript/ESM port for modern Node.js, written by Sam Liebl.
    https://github.com/stliebl/goose-ts

